FILE-12: read every token on an input line

gettokens() stops after MAXTOKS (40) tokens and drops the rest of the
line without an error, so a [PATTERNS] line with more than 39 factors,
or a [REPORT] NODES line with more than 39 IDs, was silently cut short.
The documented limit is 1,024 characters per line, so MAXTOKS is raised
to MAXLINE / 2 + 1, enough for a full line of one-character tokens.
gettokens() used to set all MAXTOKS slots to NULL for every line; it now
clears only the slots the previous line used (the others are already
NULL), so the larger array does not slow down reading the file.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-12_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/input2.c b/src/input2.c
index 220c757..bb9fd21 100644
--- a/src/input2.c
+++ b/src/input2.c
@@ -565,8 +565,9 @@ int  gettokens(char *s, char** Tok, int maxToks, char *comment)
     // clear comment
     comment[0] = '\0';
 
-    // Begin with no tokens
-    for (n=0; n<maxToks; n++) Tok[n] = NULL;
+    // Begin with no tokens (only the slots used by the previous
+    // line need clearing; the rest are still NULL)
+    for (n = 0; n < maxToks && Tok[n] != NULL; n++) Tok[n] = NULL;
     n = 0;
 
     // Truncate s at start of comment
diff --git a/src/types.h b/src/types.h
index b35c5cd..96353dd 100755
--- a/src/types.h
+++ b/src/types.h
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@ typedef  int          INT4;
 #define   MAXMSG    255      // Max. # characters in message text
 #define   MAXLINE   1024     // Max. # characters read from input line
 #define   MAXFNAME  259      // Max. # characters in file name
-#define   MAXTOKS   40       // Max. items per line of input
+#define   MAXTOKS   (MAXLINE / 2 + 1) // Max. items per line of input
 #define   TRUE      1
 #define   FALSE     0
 #define   FULL      2
